            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I installed `v0.13.0-nightly+c7f83f9`, but now:\n1. Opening a file in any way doesn't trigger the diagnostics - I tried `vim filename`, `:e`, opening with `nvim-tree` (regular and preview).\n2. `checkhealth vim.lsp` doesn't show any issues.\n3. Manually running `:lua vim.lsp.diagnostic._refresh(vim.api.nvim_get_current_buf(), vim.lsp.get_clients()[1].id, true)` shows the diagnostics\n4. Calling `vim.lsp.diagnostic._refresh` in the LSP `on_attach` function also triggers the diagnostics\n\nIt seems to be another issue now with this neovim version. I tried overwriting the `vim.lsp.diagnostic._enable` function so that it calls the original, but also sets an autocmd for `LspNotify` event. The autocmd doesn't get called, but it does if I set it outside of `_enable`. That leads me to believe that `LspNotify` `textDocument/didOpen` was executed before the autocmd created in `vim.lsp.diagnostic._enable`\n\nEDIT:\n@justinmk Yeah it seems 54188fa removed the schedule of `LspNotify` autocmd execution, but now in `Client:on_attach` `_text_document_did_open_handler` causes the `textDocument/didOpen` to be called instantly. The execution order becomes:\n1. `self:_text_document_did_open_handler(bufnr)` -> `self:notify('textDocument/didOpen'...`\n2. `lsp._set_defaults(self, bufnr)` -> `lsp.diagnostic._enable(bufnr)` -> creates LspNotify autocmd that listens for `didOpen`, but too late.\n\nA simple solution would be to move the `lsp._set_defaults(self, bufnr)` line before `self:_text_document_did_open_handler(bufnr)` in `Client:on_attach`, but I'm not sure if that wouldn't break something. Also in the future it would be very possible to introduce a `vim.schedule` somewhere due to whatever reason and that will cause a regression again.\nMore robust solution is probably to pass `client` to `vim.lsp.diagnostic._enable`, remove the autocmd for `LspNotify` and just call directly:\n```lua\nif bufstates[bufnr] and bufstates[bufnr].pull_kind == 'document' then\n  M._refresh(bufnr, client.id, true)\nend\n```\n",
