        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@jdrouhard Before creating the issue I tried with LuaLS too and indeed, the problem is not occurring with that LSP, because it doesn't support the `textDocument/diagnostic` method (it uses `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` instead). Therefore `vim.lsp.diagnostic._enable()` never gets called in `lsp._set_defaults` for LuaLS. If you try with the eslint LSP however you'll see the problem occurring (due to it using `textDocument/diagnostic`).\n\nBefore the 54188fa commit, the bug was due to the `vim.schedule` of LspNotify event execution in `Client:notify` (hence the wrong bufnr later on). You fixed this with your commit, but the bug moved elsewhere now.\n\nAfter the 54188fa commit, the bug is due to LspNotify `textDocument/didOpen` being already executed in `_text_document_did_open_handler` which is before `lsp._set_defaults` (and therefore `lsp.diagnostic._enable`). This causes the LspNotify autocmd in `lsp.diagnostic._enable` to never get triggered. This is not a regression, it's just that the logic in `lsp.diagnostic._enable` needed to be changed in the first place.\n\nAs for the solution you proposed, I think it would be better to at first only move `_set_defaults()` before `_text_document_did_open_handler` (or my other solution at the end of my previous comment) in order to fix the issue.\nOnly after that as a separate feature should the rest of your suggestions be implemented. Otherwise the bugfix is tied to the refactor of lsp diagnostics being converted to separate lsp capability.",
